# Registry profile every end-to-end lane layers over its registries' own:
# ACTIVE_PROFILES=<registry>,payments-lane. The full local stack never loads it.
#
# It recommends the one dispute authority the lanes pin, restating
# tools/payments-lane-double/fixtures/dispute-authority.toml as a one-item JSON
# array, single-quoted so the registry's dotenv reader takes it literally; a
# repository test holds the two equal. A public development value, never for a
# public network: nobody can act as that authority (the fixture says why).
# Sellers use registry recommendations by default and the lanes' buyer profile
# opts in, so no storefront or buyer configuration names a [[Dispute]] entry.
REGISTRY_DESCRIPTOR_RECOMMENDED_DISPUTE_AUTHORITIES='[{"account":"00000000-0000-4000-8000-0000000000d1","advertisement":{"mechanisms":["arkhai.payments.v1"],"minimum_dispute_window_seconds":0},"interface":"arkhai.mediation.v1","origin":"https://dispute.invalid","params":{},"record_key":"ed25519:lMg0OhYvDsBJf2G3MtLHgbPX3spRLUCV20o7HY7AFOI"}]'
